 ## Background
-TexGS-VolVis is the first 2DGS-based framework in VolVis aimed at expressive scene editing. It builds upon existing NeRF and 3DGS scene editing approaches [6, 7, 9, 22] guided by text instructions. The method was introduced in the paper "TexGS-VolVis: Expressive Scene Editing for Volume Visualization via Textured Gaussian Splatting" [S1]. It addresses the challenges of applying iterative editing strategies to complex and semi-transparent VolVis scenes, which often result in blurry appearances or geometry-inconsistent edits [S1].
+TexGS-VolVis is the first 2DGS-based framework in VolVis aimed at expressive scene editing [S1]. It builds upon existing NeRF and 3DGS scene editing approaches guided by text instructions [S1]. The method was introduced in the paper "TexGS-VolVis: Expressive Scene Editing for Volume Visualization via Textured Gaussian Splatting" [S1]. It addresses the challenges of applying iterative editing strategies to complex and semi-transparent VolVis scenes, which often result in blurry appearances or geometry-inconsistent edits [S1].
 
